{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280404-reproducing-the-unreproducable","id":1280404,"title":"Reproducing the Unreproducable","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-12T14:57:16-08:00","id":1280404,"title":"Reproducing the Unreproducable","content":"This is a thread for speculation. Here we discuss the actions, ideas and aesthetics of concepts from media and our imaginations that seem to not be represented mechanically in Exalted, that we would like to see.<br /> <br /> If you see an idea expressed here, and know of either a published mechanic that can reproduce the effect, or an \u2018ask the devs\u2019 response, please quote and provide links.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24172-sticks","name":"Sticks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T15:01:42-08:00","id":1280405,"title":"","content":"Caveats:<br /> <br /> -Exalted is pretty good about providing a broad base for us players and storytellers to work with, and our most powerful tool for this is the Stunt. Before posting, be sure your imagined mechanic can\u2019t be reproduced through creative stunting.<br /> -We all have ideas for things we would like to see, some more ambitious than others. Be sure to treat others with respect, and keep criticism constructive.<br /> -It is entirely possible that your desired mechanic simply has not been published yet. We still only have one complete book for 3E at this point, so don\u2019t give up hope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24172-sticks","name":"Sticks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T15:09:21-08:00","id":1280406,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll start us off.<br /> <br /> I haven\u2019t given the core book more than one read-through, and have since only cherry-picked for information, so it\u2019s entirely possible I have missed this. I cannot think of a way to mechanically reproduce struggles with energy projection. A classic example for anime fans are the Beamstruggles of the Dragonball franchise. How would one replicate such a thing? Would a beam be a straight mote expenditure? If so, would the person better-able to spend notes win every time? Would there be caps on how many notes were spent? Would beam-power be a balancing act of mote totals and spending-caps? Do beamstruggles have a place in Exalted? What do ya\u2019ll think?<br /> <br /> And as an example of \u2018asked-and-answered\u2019, I was somewhat annoyed to find that there were no mechanics for weapon-breakage in combat. No weapons designed to shatter your opponent\u2019s weapon, no martial-arts that specialized in punching a blade in half...but then two charms were added in Earth Dragon style, and while they require the practitioner to be a Dragonblooded, the devs said that it would not be unreasonable to create duplicate MA or even crafting charms as custom non-terrestrial variants. So there\u2019s that problem solved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24172-sticks","name":"Sticks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T15:25:11-08:00","id":1280410,"title":"","content":"What part of beam-struggles do you feel wouldn't be sufficiently represented by the clash rules?<br /> <br /> Also, Miracles of the Solar Exalted added Shattering Clash which can also destroy weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T17:58:42-08:00","id":1280422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280404-reproducing-the-unreproducable?p=1280410#post1280410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What part of beam-struggles do you feel wouldn't be sufficiently represented by the clash rules?<br /> <br /> Also, Miracles of the Solar Exalted added Shattering Clash which can also destroy weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to assume the sustained effort. And that's...harder as a narrative conceit, because the structure of Exalted doesn't lend itself to several mechanical underpinnings. The closest it has (sustained assault, extreme damage, requires time to invoke) is Death Ray, which can't really be whipped up as a quick response to someone else's Death Ray, nor do I think there's a rule for when two people Death Ray each other aside from lots of red mist in all directions. Also, it's limited to characters with Solar Circle Sorcery.<br /> <br /> None of this is a solution, obviously. Just clarifying the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T19:58:22-08:00","id":1280438,"title":"","content":"Beam struggle; (not tested, initial thoughts)<br /> <br /> Extended Clash. This optional rule can help replicate anything from two large energy attacks pressing against each other to two sword wizards locking blades and trying to push each other away to make a decisive follow up. <br /> <br /> When two attacks clash as per the usual rules, compare the threshold successes to the loser\u2019s defence. If it is lower, the winner gains a number of initiative equal to the difference and struggle continues for another round, if it is higher the winner\u2019s attack pushes through with all the usual results of a successful clash attack. <br /> <br /> Each round the clash continues, both characters lose 2i and are at -2 defence against any other attacks against them from additional characters. <br /> <br /> <br /> Assisted Extended Clash;<br /> A character locked in an extended clash can receive assistance from an ally. Resolving this assistance is done on the same way, compare all competing attacks against each other and grant initiative accordingly, or break the struggle once even one character\u2019s defence is overcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T05:55:09-08:00","id":1280464,"title":"","content":"I like these ideas, and I\u2019ll have to look at Shattering Clash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24172-sticks","name":"Sticks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T04:01:56-08:00","id":1281075,"title":"","content":"Terminator Armour.<br /> I'm struggling to convey a sense of 'weight' I've found that Super Heavy Armour didn't cut it and a human sized Warstrider ran into a different problem where it seemed way too easy to damage it. I'm prepared for most of it's power to be in the Evocations but the base traits just feel lacking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T07:50:33-08:00","id":1281094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280404-reproducing-the-unreproducable?p=1281075#post1281075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Terminator Armour.<br /> I'm struggling to convey a sense of 'weight' I've found that Super Heavy Armour didn't cut it and a human sized Warstrider ran into a different problem where it seemed way too easy to damage it. I'm prepared for most of it's power to be in the Evocations but the base traits just feel lacking.</div> </div> </div> </div>My solution to &quot;smaller warstrider&quot; was to split health-level damage between the armor and the person underneath (with a remaining health level going to the armor).<br /> <br /> This represents the superior level of protection relative to other armors AND the inferior level of protection compared to a warstrider, and makes the armor harder to damage than a warstrider while more demanding to employ than &quot;regular&quot; magical armor.<br /> <br /> It's also important to remember that the armor doesn't need to be First Age Artifice, so it can be more easily repaired than a warstrider, using Craft: Artifact instead of Craft: First Age Artifice, and perhaps with fewer resources required.<br /> <br /> I think this represents &quot;weight&quot; because these ablative health levels would be the armor's first Evocation, rather than anything which would make it less encumbering or more agile.<br /> <br /> I don't think you'd actually want to represent weight with GREATER mobility penalties and new restrictions on movement actions, at least outside of an Evocation that balanced those weaknesses with great strengths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T07:56:59-08:00","id":1281097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280404-reproducing-the-unreproducable?p=1280410#post1280410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What part of beam-struggles do you feel wouldn't be sufficiently represented by the clash rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Talking is a free action&quot;.<br /> <br /> Normally, characters in <i>Exalted </i>have a limit on how much they can say per round, let alone per tick, but a clash happens in a single instant of one tick, while Luke and Vader can have an entire conversation while struggling to see who wins a lightsaber clash.<br /> <br /> In that regard, it's more like two characters Grappling each other, except neither chooses to Savage the other. Maybe the one who wins initiative each round always Restrains the other? But if the first to establish a clinch chooses to Restrain, then the other couldn't counter-Grapple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T09:16:22-08:00","id":1281114,"title":"","content":"I think the give and take of initiative would be the struggle part of the beam clash, although you'd need two people that have some sort of beam attack.<br /> <br /> Round 1, either someone delays or by chance they launch their beam attacks for a (preferably) withering clash. It's been too long for me to recall the specifics of the various beam attacks. Hopefully they aren't all decisive only.<br /> Someone wins the clash, and either buying in to the conceit, or by not winning enough initiative to comfortably Decisive Beam clash next round, they delay and clash again for Round 2.<br /> <br /> Because of how clashes work when one person is Withering and the other is Decisiving (I formally apologize to the English language for what I just did to it), even if the Round 1 clash was enough for the winner to want to Decisive attack, they are at a slight disadvantage, and the beam struggle could swing the other way.<br /> <br /> Even if they don't buy in for a second round of beam clash, that even works in the fiction, they intentionally break beam struggle dodge, and fire again since they have the advantage.<br /> <br /> All you need are two players with Beam abilities and a bit of savvy around the combat system. DBs would be easy because everyone can dip for Elemental Bolt, but I don't remember the Solar options beyond the Brawl one and GSB.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T09:51:52-08:00","id":1281119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280404-reproducing-the-unreproducable?p=1281097#post1281097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Talking is a free action&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Normally, characters in <i>Exalted </i>have a limit on how much they can say per round, let alone per tick, but a clash happens in a single instant of one tick, while Luke and Vader can have an entire conversation while struggling to see who wins a lightsaber clash.<br /> <br /> In that regard, it's more like two characters Grappling each other, except neither chooses to Savage the other. Maybe the one who wins initiative each round always Restrains the other? But if the first to establish a clinch chooses to Restrain, then the other couldn't counter-Grapple.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not perfect, but this is another thing kind of covered in Miracles. &quot;Talking is a free action&quot; to me is more Wesley vs Inigo. A pleasant conversation while trying to kill each other. Proper social actions (instill/persuade/etc) require a flurry. In the case of Darth Vader vs Luke, Vader is clearly squinting with both social and physical attacks, and the charm Poised Lion Attitude allows you to take full social actions as a free action rather than a flurry for 3m.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T10:51:07-08:00","id":1281130,"title":"","content":"If you have opponents who both preferentially clash when the opportunity presents itself, then you could easily stunt each new clash they make as an extension of the old one, locking swords or beams or what have you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T11:09:28-08:00","id":1281133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280404-reproducing-the-unreproducable?p=1281130#post1281130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have opponents who both preferentially clash when the opportunity presents itself, then you could easily stunt each new clash they make as an extension of the old one, locking swords or beams or what have you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the &quot;ongoing clash&quot; idea works pretty well for both &quot;beam struggles&quot; and stuff like duels. However, I'd like to see some mechanical incentive, both for participants in such clashes to engage with them, and to have other people leave them alone. Therefore, a couple of ideas for house rules for that. <br /> <br /> 1) If you were in a clash last turn, you can waive the init cost to delay your action, as long as you again clash with the same target (if you choose to do something else, you must pay the init cost).<br /> <br /> 2) Every round you clash someone, as long as no one else has attacked them in the turn since then, your reward from winning the clash increases. For a withering attack, your base initiative gain (that is the 1 init you get from any successful withering attack) increases by 1 for each round you maintain the clash (if you won the clash on the 2nd turn of clashing by 5, for example, you'd gain 7 initiative. Your opponent would still only lose 5, though). On a decisive attack, for every round you've maintained the clash past the first, you can treat the opponent's Hardness as 1 lower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T11:55:25-08:00","id":1281142,"title":"","content":"You could also write a social Charm that specifically allows you to engage a target in a philosophical debate that violates the laws of time, as long as you're engaging them in a clash.<br /> <br /> Whoever wins the debate wins the clash, or at least gains an advantage towards winning it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T09:51:09-08:00","id":1281318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280404-reproducing-the-unreproducable?p=1281094#post1281094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My solution to &quot;smaller warstrider&quot; was to split health-level damage between the armor and the person underneath (with a remaining health level going to the armor).<br /> <br /> This represents the superior level of protection relative to other armors AND the inferior level of protection compared to a warstrider, and makes the armor harder to damage than a warstrider while more demanding to employ than &quot;regular&quot; magical armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has potential. Thanks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you'd actually want to represent weight with GREATER mobility penalties and new restrictions on movement actions, at least outside of an Evocation that balanced those weaknesses with great strengths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... if you followed armour traits to the next logical progression +14 soak, hardness 13, mobility -3 attune 7 the problem was twofold.<br /> -Character in heavy armour are already making an informed decision to favour soak over mobility and evasion in a way that'll likely be reflected in their charm and trait purchases , so superheavy armour would just have even better soak for sacrifices that the heavy armour wearer has probably already made. <br /> -It's very lackluster for terminator armour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T14:43:43-08:00","id":1281379,"title":"","content":"Okay, now <i>I</i> want help.<br /> <br /> Without using an artifact or its Evocations, how the fuck does a character use a two-handed hammer to smash someone as hard as Solar Brawl's Heaven Thunder Hammer or Terrestrial Brawl's Firmament-Shattering Impact?<br /> <br /> A decisive attack that knocks the target out of the range band, prone, and inflicts falling damage upon them. Potentially smashing a target through destructible walls.<br /> <br /> Strength-boosting Athletics Charms may or may not be involved to achieve this result.<br /> <br /> <br /> Every single Volume of <i>RWBY</i>, Nora Valkyrie fucking NAILS something so hard with her hammer that it usually vacates her presence and changes the landscape in its new zipcode. Even when she was using a watermelon on a stick rather than her &quot;artifact&quot; weapon, Magnhild.<br /> <br /> Finding a balance point between the amazingly accessible HTH and the very inaccessible FSS has been a source of extreme frustration, especially when trying to balance those Brawl Charms against a Martial Arts Charm which can only be used with a heavy, two-handed hammer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 01-17-2019, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T15:43:42-08:00","id":1281385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280404-reproducing-the-unreproducable?p=1281379#post1281379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, now <i>I</i> want help.<br /> <br /> Without using an artifact or its Evocations, how the fuck does a character use a two-handed hammer to smash someone as hard as Solar Brawl's Heaven Thunder Hammer or Terrestrial Brawl's Firmament-Shattering Impact?<br /> <br /> A decisive attack that knocks the target out of the range band, prone, and inflicts falling damage upon them. Potentially smashing a target through destructible walls.<br /> <br /> Strength-boosting Athletics Charms may or may not be involved to achieve this result.<br /> <br /> <br /> Every single Volume of <i>RWBY</i>, Nora Valkyrie fucking NAILS something so hard with her hammer that it usually vacates her presence and changes the landscape in its new zipcode. Even when she was using a watermelon on a stick rather than her &amp;quot;artifact&amp;quot; weapon, Magnhild.<br /> <br /> Finding a balance point between the amazingly accessible HTH and the very inaccessible FSS has been a source of extreme frustration, especially when trying to balance those Brawl Charms against a Martial Arts Charm which can only be used with a heavy, two-handed hammer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like pretty fertile ground for a martial art to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T19:32:29-08:00","id":1281427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280404-reproducing-the-unreproducable?p=1281385#post1281385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like pretty fertile ground for a martial art to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not good enough to write it, and I've been trying, on and off, <i>for years.</i><br /> <br /> I might have stumbled on a decent Form Charm design, but I still don't understand the underlying mechanical weights of the system enough to have an answer to Heaven Thunder Hammer and Firmament-Shattering Strike.<br /> <br /> I don't count Earth Dragon's Avalanche Method, because that doubles as a flurry-attack Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T08:09:25-08:00","id":1281511,"title":"","content":"*spitball*<br /> <br /> <b>Hammer of Thundering Heaven</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 7m; <b>Mins:</b> Melee 4, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-only, Heavy-only, Enhanced-Smashing<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Fire and Stones Strike<br /> <br /> Leveraging the mass and momentum of her weapon, the Lawgiver brings down the full force of Heaven upon her foe.<br /> <br /> (HTH goes here)<br /> <br /> When using a weapon with the Smashing tag, add 1 to your damage roll for the purposes of calculating how far your target is struck.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> Charms with the Heavy-Only keyword may only be used when you are using a Heavy melee weapon; Light and Medium weapons lack sufficient heft and length to make effective use with these magics.<br /> <br /> Charms with the Enhanced keyword have an additional effect or other bonus when used with a melee weapon that carries that keyword.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T14:06:43-08:00","id":1281574,"title":"","content":"Melee Charms are supposed to apply universally to all Melee weapons, without specializing in particular ones, I do believe.<br /> <br /> We have more Melee Charms than ever before for Ability-based Exalted, and none of them get specific like your proposal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T18:53:08-08:00","id":1281605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280404-reproducing-the-unreproducable?p=1281574#post1281574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Melee Charms are supposed to apply universally to all Melee weapons, without specializing in particular ones, I do believe.<br /> <br /> We have more Melee Charms than ever before for Ability-based Exalted, and none of them get specific like your proposal.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're saying that your idea inspired a potential new well of design space!<br /> <br /> More seriously, the conceit that every melee charm must always be equally applicable with every melee weapon, from a knife to a great grandmaul, is a bit silly. Different weapons lend themselves to different styles of combat. A Solar using a big fuckoff hammer should be able to knock people away in a fashion that would look pretty silly if that Solar was using a stilleto.<br /> <br /> Something not having been done before is insufficient as an argument against it, unless you can demonstrate an underlying principle for why it hasn't been done before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T13:50:37-08:00","id":1281810,"title":"","content":"if you want a charm that is specific to only one type of weapon, then just make it an evocation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T14:28:22-08:00","id":1281823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280404-reproducing-the-unreproducable?p=1281810#post1281810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if you want a charm that is specific to only one type of weapon, then just make it an evocation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The character concept is someone who can Heaven Thunder Hammer someone with even an improvised mundane weapon.<br /> <br /> Do you feel like this isn't the sort of thing that any Exalt with a hammer should be able to do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T15:39:35-08:00","id":1281830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280404-reproducing-the-unreproducable?p=1281823#post1281823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The character concept is someone who can Heaven Thunder Hammer someone with even an improvised mundane weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read Heaven Thunder Hammer again; there's nothing in there barring you from using it with an improvised weapon. I'd argue the text does more to forbid you from doling out a Heaven Thunder Hammer with a headbutt than it does a watermelon on a stick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280404-reproducing-the-unreproducable?p=1281823#post1281823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you feel like this isn't the sort of thing that any Exalt with a hammer should be able to do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because <i>an</i> Exalt develops a custom Charm, doesn't mean just <i>any</i> Exalt of the same splat will come up with the same trick.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut anyway, the solution I used in my seafaring game for resolving a similar issue was that Barbus took a Permanent Evocation from his warclub that let him treat all manner of clubs and hammers as if they had the Brawl tag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-20-2019, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T07:16:25-08:00","id":1282284,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m still trying to make a charm that allows for thematic destruction without resorting to writing every stunt the exact same way. Think Anji from Rurouni Kenshin. <br /> <br /> I described the character concept to my ST, and he said \u2018Well, Shattering Grasp from Craft kinda does that.\u2019 So since then I have been trying to make this work consistently and systematically without needing to re-write the same stunt again and again. The problem is that my ST insists (rightly so) that craft charms are not combat charms, and that I shouldn\u2019t try to fit a square peg into a round hole.<br /> <br /> I tried going deeper into craft/sorcery, talking about destroying something on a fundamental level, taking an understanding of how creation works and how to break it...buuut the ST said that sounded more Sidereal than Solar.<br /> <br /> Any ideas for a combat-capable charm that emphasizes destroying things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24172-sticks","name":"Sticks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T07:54:55-08:00","id":1282286,"title":"","content":"<b>Double Layer Limit</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m; <b>Mins:</b> Brawl 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Dual, Bridge<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Fists of Iron Technique OR Shattering Grasp<br /> <br /> With precisely focused violence, even the most powerful defenses must fall.<br /> <br /> When a Withering attack enhanced with Double Layer Limit hits, the victim subtracts his current Onslaught penalty from his soak, to a minimum of 0. This penalty remains for the remainder of combat. If struck by multiple uses of Double Layer Limit, only the greatest penalty applies.<br /> <br /> When a Decisive attack enhanced with Double Layer Limit hits, the victim subtracts his current Onslaught penalty from his hardness, to a minimum of 0. This penalty remains for the remainder of combat. If struck by multiple uses of Double Layer Limit, only the greatest penalty applies. If the victim has no Hardness, this instead adds a number of decisive damage dice equal to the penalty it would have imposed, but only for this attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Shattering Land</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 6m, 3i; <b>Mins:</b> Brawl 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Withering-only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Double Layer Limit<br /> <br /> Against the fury of the Lawgivers, the very stone and soil of the earth must give way.<br /> <br /> By using Shattering Land, the Solar directs a powerful series of strikes into the ground at her feet, resulting in an explosion of dust and debris. Make a (Strength + Brawl) <b>Withering</b> attack against everyone at Close range; the base damage from this attack does not benefit from your Strength, and may be soaked normally.<br /> <br /> In the after-effects of using Shattering Land, the area around the Solar is broken and difficult to traverse, qualifying as difficult terrain (p. 199). The Storyteller may add additional consequences; using Shattering Land should not be enough to bring down a sturdy building, but may cause a crumbling ruin to begin to collapse, take down a bridge or precarious crossing, or create a hole that drops everyone down a floor.<br /> <br /> Shattering Land may only be used once per scene.<br /> <br /> At Essence 3, you may purchase Shattering Land a second time; by spending an additional Willpower when using Shattering Land, you may cause the explosion to occur at a location out to Short range. At Essence 5, you may purchase Shattering Land a third and final time, increasing the range to Medium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T08:25:14-08:00","id":1282433,"title":"","content":"Wastevens, I love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24172-sticks","name":"Sticks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T08:53:52-08:00","id":1282441,"title":"","content":"I'l admit to not having watched much Kenshin, but Sledgehammer Fist Punch is pretty handy for casual destruction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T11:37:18-08:00","id":1282469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280404-reproducing-the-unreproducable?p=1281830#post1281830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Read Heaven Thunder Hammer again; there's nothing in there barring you from using it with an improvised weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>But why would you?<br /> <br /> And what if your character concept involves no unarmed attacking at all? A hammer-centric, Brawl-forsaking character investing three dots into Brawl just to access a common hammer trick just doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just because <i>an</i> Exalt develops a custom Charm, doesn't mean just <i>any</i> Exalt of the same splat will come up with the same trick. </div> </div> </div>And yet, there are Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bBut anyway, the solution I used in my seafaring game for resolving a similar issue was that Barbus took a Permanent Evocation from his warclub that let him treat all manner of clubs and hammers as if they had the Brawl tag. </div> </div> </div>Solars absorbing Evocations from their artifacts is an idea that didn't make it into the final publication, and I'm glad for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T11:38:59-08:00","id":1282471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280404-reproducing-the-unreproducable?p=1282441#post1282441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'l admit to not having watched much Kenshin, but Sledgehammer Fist Punch is pretty handy for casual destruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that is the intention, but I've always been confused about how it works, mechanically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T12:48:29-08:00","id":1282485,"title":"","content":"Sledgehammer Fist Punch does let you tear up the terrain really well, insofar as performing Feats of Destruction goes. But Anji in Kenshin is more of a 'precisely placed power penetrates pointless protection' element. Plus, he makes the ground explode by punching it. And then later, makes the ground explode at a distance by throwing a little knife.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T17:20:53-08:00","id":1282552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280404-reproducing-the-unreproducable?p=1282469#post1282469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But why would you?</div> </div> </div> </div>You were the one who specified being able to use a Heaven Thunder Hammer-type effect using an improvised weapon such as a watermelon on a stick. I was just the one who pointed out that you can already use Heaven Thunder Hammer using a watermelon on a stick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280404-reproducing-the-unreproducable?p=1282469#post1282469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what if your character concept involves no unarmed attacking at all?<br /> <br /> A hammer-centric, Brawl-forsaking character investing three dots into Brawl just to access a common hammer trick just doesn't make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet one of the best dips in the system is to invest three dots into Brawl just to access Thunderclap Rush Attack, even if you never plan to throw a punch with the character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280404-reproducing-the-unreproducable?p=1282469#post1282469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet, there are Martial Arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, which are both discrete and reproducible by entire other Exalt types.<br /> <br /> (And just noting, even if you never intend on throwing a punch with the character, even weapon-centric Martial Arts require a small investment in Brawl.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280404-reproducing-the-unreproducable?p=1282469#post1282469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars absorbing Evocations from their artifacts is an idea that didn't make it into the final publication, and I'm glad for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Check again. Per the Core, &quot;<b>Unless otherwise specified</b>, characters can only use Evocations while wielding or wearing the associated weapon or suit of armor.&quot; The writers <i>absolutely </i>left a space in the system for Evocations that benefit the Exalt without the artifact at hand (even if none have been published yet).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-24-2019, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T07:16:28-08:00","id":1282632,"title":"","content":"It doesn\u2019t help that Solar Brawl is simply the most powerful default melee combat style, or that it is incompatable with the Martial Arts that require it.<br /> <br /> Our game started with a MA tournament, so every character had MA as their primary combat ability. Our ST waived the Brawl requirements so we wouldn\u2019t be so limited, but now I\u2019m in a pickle with charm creation.<br /> <br /> BTW, my group\u2019s consensus was that Double-Layer limit is well-built, but a bit underpowered without its prerequisite Brawl charms as it extends the onslaught-Brawl tree. Shattering Land was deemed very good and very interesting, but it needs a cap on the amount of initiative that can be gained. Figured either a low maximum of initiative gained per target, or only gaining the highest single gain from one opponent. Really like the repurchase upgrades.<br /> Thanks again for putting those out. I feel like you really captured the spirit of what I was going for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24172-sticks","name":"Sticks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T13:17:59-08:00","id":1284194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what if your character concept involves no unarmed attacking at all? A hammer-centric, Brawl-forsaking character investing three dots into Brawl just to access a common hammer trick just doesn't make sense. </div> </div> </div>here's my try on a melee charm that might help/ inspire you to achieve what your after. all this without breaking the &quot; melee charms must apply to all types of weapons&quot;:<br /> <br /> <b>FIRST LIGHT OF THE DAY STRIKE</b><br /> <b>cost</b>: 4m, 1wp <b>mins</b>: Melee 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type</b>: supplemental<br /> <b>Keyword</b>: Perilous<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms</b>: Fire and Stone Strike<br /> <br /> <i>The solar's weapon surges with burning essence, empowering its natural effectiveness to reach new heights.</i><br /> This charm supplements a non-gambit attack made using the TAG of a weapon. these effect are added to the normal Tag description<br /> ( example: smashing medium. -1 ef, -2 ini. knock opponents 2 range band)<br /> <br /> <u>Smashing</u>: Light and medium weapons gain +1 range band or short fall damage if knocked prone; heavy weapon gain +2 range band or medium fall damage if knocked prone.<br /> <br /> <u>Piercing</u>: Light and medium weapons gain +1 to soak value; heavy weapon gain +2 to soak value<br /> <br /> <u>Chopping</u>: Light and medium weapons gain +1 withering dmg and to hardness value; heavy weapon gain +2 withering dmg and to hardness value<br /> <br /> <b>Essence 4+</b>: you no longuer suffer a defence penalty or initiative cost to activate these Tag when using this charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23883-devaking","name":"devaking","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T08:02:18-08:00","id":1286710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>devaking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280404-reproducing-the-unreproducable?p=1284194#post1284194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> here's my try on a melee charm that might help/ inspire you to achieve what your after. all this without breaking the &quot; melee charms must apply to all types of weapons&quot;:<br /> <br /> <b>FIRST LIGHT OF THE DAY STRIKE</b><br /> <b>cost</b>: 4m, 1wp <b>mins</b>: Melee 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type</b>: supplemental<br /> <b>Keyword</b>: Perilous<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms</b>: Fire and Stone Strike<br /> <br /> <i>The solar's weapon surges with burning essence, empowering its natural effectiveness to reach new heights.</i><br /> This charm supplements a non-gambit attack made using the TAG of a weapon. these effect are added to the normal Tag description<br /> ( example: smashing medium. -1 ef, -2 ini. knock opponents 2 range band)<br /> <br /> <u>Smashing</u>: Light and medium weapons gain +1 range band or short fall damage if knocked prone; heavy weapon gain +2 range band or medium fall damage if knocked prone.<br /> <br /> <u>Piercing</u>: Light and medium weapons gain +1 to soak value; heavy weapon gain +2 to soak value<br /> <br /> <u>Chopping</u>: Light and medium weapons gain +1 withering dmg and to hardness value; heavy weapon gain +2 withering dmg and to hardness value<br /> <br /> <b>Essence 4+</b>: you no longuer suffer a defence penalty or initiative cost to activate these Tag when using this charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this or something like it seem acceptable.<br /> <br /> Otherwise a Charm that allows knockdown with any Melee weapon, which is more effective if that weapon has the smashing tag and is used for a smashing attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}